Size the cheat parser's group buffer for its terminator

retro_cheat_set copies each hexadecimal group of a cheat into a stack array
of exactly the group's length, then writes the terminating NUL one byte past
its end: a one-byte stack overflow for every group of every cheat applied.
The array gets the one byte it needs.

Applied at build time by Vendor/n64-ios/build.sh, after 0002. Worth sending
upstream.

--- a/libretro/libretro.c
+++ b/libretro/libretro.c
@@ -2293,7 +2293,7 @@
             matchLength++;
         } else {
             if (matchLength){
-               char codePartS[matchLength];
+               char codePartS[matchLength + 1];
                strncpy(codePartS,codeLine+cursor-matchLength,matchLength);
                codePartS[matchLength]=0;
                codeParts[partCount++]=strtoul(codePartS,NULL,16);
